            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"check-2-small-cells\">Check 2 \u2014 Small cells</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A count small enough can point at a handful of people. CMS's public files suppress small counts \u2014 this is <strong>CMS's cell-size suppression convention; confirm the current policy</strong> before you cite a number. You can see it in the data: in the HRRP file the smallest <em>Number of Readmissions</em> shown is <strong>11</strong>, and <strong>3,683</strong> rows say \"Too Few to Report\" instead. The default threshold here is 11 to match what the data shows; set your own if your policy differs. Zeros are listed separately: decide whether a zero in your layer could identify anyone.</span></span><marimo-ui-element object-id='Xref-0' random-id='4f629d6f-04be-706e-53eb-381d1cd1f9c3'><marimo-table data-initial-value='[]' data-label='null' data-data='&quot;[{&#92;&quot;count column&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Number of Discharges&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;cells with a number&#92;&quot;:8242,&#92;&quot;cells from 1 to 10&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;cells equal to 0&#92;&quot;:205,&#92;&quot;smallest non-zero&#92;&quot;:27.0},{&#92;&quot;count column&#92;&quot;:&#92;&quot;Number of Readmissions&#92;&quot;,&#92;&quot;cells with a number&#92;&quot;:8037,&#92;&quot;cells from 1 to 10&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;cells equal to 0&#92;&quot;:0,&#92;&quot;smallest non-zero&#92;&quot;:11.0}]&quot;' data-total-rows='2' data-total-columns='5' data-max-columns='50' data-banner-text='&quot;&quot;' data-pagination='false' data-page-size='10' data-field-types='[[&quot;count column&quot;,[&quot;string&quot;,&quot;str&quot;]],[&quot;cells with a number&quot;,[&quot;integer&quot;,&quot;int64&quot;]],[&quot;cells from 1 to 10&quot;,[&quot;integer&quot;,&quot;int64&quot;]],[&quot;cells equal to 0&q